# The Powell Lab / sceQTL-Gen legacy that much of this workflow is adapted from is
# credited in the `references:` block below (and in the abstract), which is the
# standard way to credit derived work. The Zenodo concept DOI is added under
# `identifiers:` once the v1.0.0 GitHub release mints it.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this workflow, please cite it using the metadata below."
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-16"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.23405367"
    description: "Concept DOI (resolves to the latest version)"
title: "imputation: a genotype QC and 1000 Genomes imputation Snakemake workflow"
abstract: >-
  A Snakemake workflow that takes measured genotypes (VCF) and performs quality
  control (sample filtering, a sex check, and ancestry checks against a 1000
  Genomes reference) and imputation of missing variants against a 1000 Genomes reference
  panel, followed by filtering to produce SNP profiles suitable for single-cell
  demultiplexing with Demuxafy. Much of the pipeline is adapted directly from the
  Powell Lab / sceQTL-Gen consortium imputation workflow (see references).
type: software
